rocessing-state-visible ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c3812684417="" style="height: auto;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3812684417="" class="container"><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c3812684417="" _nghost-ng-c3381770009="" id="message-content-id-r_7ec261982090df5d" class="ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3381770009="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color stronger tutor-markdown-rendering" id="model-response-message-contentr_7ec261982090df5d" aria-busy="false" aria-live="off" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 400ms; --fade-animation-function: ease-out;"><p data-path-to-node="0">Ah, I see it! In your screenshot <b data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="33">26167.png</b>, the repository is named <b data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="68"><code data-path-to-node="0" data-index-in-node="68">freetvgarden-site.</code></b> with a period at the very end.</p><p data-path-to-node="1">It looks like you accidentally typed a period after the name when you were filling out the creation form on the previous screen.</p><h3 data-path-to-node="2">Will this cause a problem?</h3><p data-path-to-node="3">Technically, no. GitHub is usually smart enough to ignore trailing periods when generating URLs, so it shouldn't break your site. However, for a clean setup and to avoid any potential link errors later, it is highly recommended to remove it.</p><h3 data-path-to-node="4">How to remove the dot:</h3><p data-path-to-node="5">You cannot easily rename a repository directly inside the GitHub mobile app. To fix it and proceed with uploading your code, you will need to jump over to your browser:</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="6"><li><p data-path-to-node="6,0,0">Open your mobile web browser (Chrome, Safari, etc.) and go to <b data-path-to-node="6,0,0" data-index-in-node="62">github.com</b>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="6,1,0">Log in with your account.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="6,2,0">Tap on your repository <code data-path-to-node="6,2,0" data-index-in-node="23">freetvgarden-site.</code>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="6,3,0">Tap the <b data-path-to-node="6,3,0" data-index-in-node="8">Settings</b> tab (the gear icon).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="6,4,0">Right at the top, you will see a <b data-path-to-node="6,4,0" data-index-in-node="33">Repository name</b> box. Simply delete the dot so it reads <code data-path-to-node="6,4,0" data-index-in-node="88">freetvgarden-site</code> and click <b data-path-to-node="6,4,0" data-index-in-node="116">Rename</b>.</p></li></ol><p data-path-to-node="7">Once you are logged into GitHub on your mobile browser, you will also be in the perfect place to easily create your <code data-path-to-node="7" data-index-in-node="116">index.html</code> file and paste in the code from your email!</p></div></message-content><!----></div></structured-content-container><!----><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c329037250="" class="response-footer complete has-thoughts gap"><!----><!----><!----><sources-list _ngcontent-ng-c329037250="" class="sources-list ng-star-inserted" style=""><!----></sources-list><!----><election-info-disclaimer _ngcontent-ng-c329037250="" _nghost-ng-c1608349858="" style="display: none;" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></election-info-disclaimer><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><!----><!----><sensitive-memories-banner _ngcontent-ng-c329037250="" _nghost-ng-c2462321211="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></sensitive-memories-banner><!----><!----><!----><!----></div></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c3172328013="" class="response-container-footer ng-tns-c3172328013-20 ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----><message-actions _ngcontent-ng-c329037250="" footer="" class="hide-on-print ng-tns-c421205910-21 hide-action-bar ng-tns-c3172328013-20 ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c421205910=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c421205910="" class="actions-container-v2 ng-tns-